<title>POLAND: Poland sells PLN 11 mln one-year bonds.</title>
<headline>Poland sells PLN 11 mln one-year bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland sold 11 million zlotys of one-year bonds after investors bid for 146 million worth of the paper at the treasury's 200 million zloty tender, the central bank said.</p>
<p>It said the minimum price of the bonds, due on June 4, 1998, fell to 92.50 from 94.48 at the previous auction of similar bonds on February 25, 1997.</p>
<p>The average price fell to 92.79 from 94.62.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
